WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.500
We are often told how loud super sonic booms
are, but rarely actually get the chance to

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.020
hear it for ourselves.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.160
One of the rare timas where a boom was heard
in an American city occurred in 2010 when

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.039
a small floatplane entered restricted airspace
over Seattle when, former US President, Barack

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:29.340
Obama was visiting.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.710
Twin F-15 Eagles were scrambled to intercept
the floatplane and in the process broke the

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.440
sound barrier over the greater Seattle area.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.110
The low flying aircraft created a boom strong
enough to shake homes and was heard as far

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:45.520
as south Washington state and caused a huge
surge in calls into local emergency services

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.520
centres.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.680
This phenomenon of sonic booms is one of the
key limiting factors that caused the Concorde

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.460
to be an economic failure, but high flying
aircraft don’t create near as loud booms

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.899
as the sound energy is dissipated as it travels
through the air.

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:03.250
The other limiting factor, preventing the
Concorde from achieving economic success was

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.640
it’s fuel economy.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.610
When comparing it to one of it’s major competitors,
the Boeing 747, it consumed about 50% more

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.600
fuel, carried a quarter the amount of passengers,
and had about half the maximum range.The range

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.920
was so poor, the plane was basically limited
to transatlantic flights as it couldn’t

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.850
cross the Pacific Ocean and and was banned
from flying over land, as a result to those

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.630
pesky sonic booms.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.460
Although the entire airplane was treated like
first class, flight tickets were still very

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.930
high compared to competitor first class offerings,
and it was difficult to find enough people

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:35.310
to pay those prices regularly.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:40.090
Although the Concorde was, for all intents
and purposes, a safe and successful aircraft

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:45.520
for the entirety of its 27 year career, there
were more than a handful of reasons the aircraft

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.920
was officially retired in 2003.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.340
Growing pressure from the British and French
governments, concerns about fuel costs, the

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.940
lack of route options and the simple shortage
of mass market potential simply killed this

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.200
iconic aircraft.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.479
For the next generation of supersonic aircraft
to succeed they are going to have to overcome

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:07.010
these challenges and this exactly what Boom
Technology plans to do.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:11.579
Boom is a startup company aiming to create
a 45-passenger civilian supersonic transport

00:02:11.579 --> 00:02:16.650
aircraft to fly up to Mach 2.2 at a price
comparable to a business class ticket on a

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.450
regular airline.The laws concerning supersonic
flight over land are still in place, so their

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:26.250
plans are currently focusing on creating economically
viable transoceanic flights.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:30.120
Like a London to New York flight that would
take just 3 hours 15 minutes with a price

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.060
of $2,500.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:38.340
A San Francisco to Tokyo flight that would
take just 5 and a half hours and cost $3,250

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:45.330
each way or an LA to Sydney route with a flight
time of 6 hours and 45 minutes at $3,500 each

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.330
way.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.780
These are still extremely expensive flights,
but they open up the possibility of getting

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:54.310
a early morning flight in LA, arrive in Tokyo
for a business meeting over Sushi and being

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.920
back in time to tuck your kids into bed.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.640
Time is money for many people.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.850
Boom are currently developing two aircraft.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:07.800
An all-premium class airliner and a geometrically
similar two seater jet called the XB-1.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.440
The XB-1 will be a 1/3rd scale demonstration
aircraft, intended to be a test bed and proof

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.160
of concept for the larger airliner

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.530
The team, don’t just have the advantage
of hindsight guiding their design.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:22.870
When the Concorde was being developed computers
weren’t really used for design work.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.400
Everything was done on paper and tested in
wind tunnels.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:30.090
Today the engineers at Boom have incredible
design software allowing them to quickly develop

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:35.450
prototype designs and have powerful computational
analysis software that can test the designs

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:40.580
the same day, without pouring money into building
a scaled prototype and paying for wind tunnel

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.580
hours.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.420
This allows them to tweak the design to the
finest detail to create the most efficient

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.730
aircraft possible.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:51.239
What once took days and thousands of dollars
to test, takes a single engineer a couple

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:52.269
of hours.

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:56.210
This coupled with carbon fibre reinforced
plastics is allowing the design of the Boom

00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:01.250
Supersonic airliner to be lightweight, be
shaped perfectly and perform well at the high

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.400
temperatures of supersonic flight.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.920
So beyond these advantages, what are the differences
between the Concorde and Boom?

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.870
Boom believe that a 30% increase in fuel efficiency
would reduce operating costs sufficiently

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.959
to allow a viable business model.

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:20.180
The Concorde consumed 16.7 litres of fuel
every 100 kilometres per passenger, but the

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:25.000
Concorde had an average passenger capacity
of about 100 with 25 rows with 4 seats in

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.000
each.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.360
Boom plan to have just 45 passengers each
getting their own window seat and aisle access.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.740
Creating a much more enjoyable experience
over the cramped interior of the Concorde,

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:40.449
but it also makes that target of a 30% decrease
in fuel consumption per passenger much more

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:41.449
difficult.

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:45.479
Let’s look at some of the design features
they are introducing to achieve this goal.

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:50.410
Both planes feature an extremely thin delta
wing, named after the triangular greek letter

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.410
delta.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:55.339
This design feature is essential to allowing
the wing to function at both subsonic and

00:04:55.339 --> 00:04:56.430
supersonic speeds.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.819
If you watched my video about Why Plane Wings
are Angled Backwards, you will understand

00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:05.059
why sweeping the wing is incredibly important
for planes that travel close to the speed

00:05:05.059 --> 00:05:09.030
of sound, but it’s important for planes
breaking the speed of sound too.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.219
As an object approaches the speed of sound
it experiences a sharp increase in coefficient

00:05:13.219 --> 00:05:18.339
of drag and as explained in my Greatest Innovations
in Formula One video the drag force on an

00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:23.960
object increases with the square of the velocity,
so creating a streamlined aircraft is incredibly

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:29.169
important for supersonic aircraft, especially
when fuel efficiency is paramount.

00:05:29.169 --> 00:05:34.339
Intuitively we want to minimise the cross-sectional
area of the aircraft to reduce drag, but we

00:05:34.339 --> 00:05:38.279
also want to minimise the changes in cross
sectional area along the length of the plane

00:05:38.279 --> 00:05:44.180
to reduce the wave drag.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:49.149
If we compare two shapes with the same maximum
cross-sectional area, but one is smoothed

00:05:49.149 --> 00:05:53.580
and other has a sudden change in cross sectional
area, we can see the later has a much high

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.629
coefficient of drag as it enters supersonic
speed.

00:05:56.629 --> 00:06:03.649
So the plane's fuselage is narrowed where
where it meets the wing, as the wing increases

00:06:03.649 --> 00:06:11.270
the cross sectional area of the plane at that
location.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.789
This is called the Area-Rule.

00:06:15.789 --> 00:06:20.179
Sweeping the wing backwards decreases the
coefficient of drag significantly at transonic

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:28.020
and supersonic speeds too and the Delta wing
allows for a sweep angle of up to 70 degrees,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:41.400
while also allowing for a very thin wing,
thanks to the large chord and short wingspan.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.770
The Delta wing performs well at low speeds
too, as a result of unique swirling vortices

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:48.159
that form on the uppers surface of the wing.

00:06:48.159 --> 00:06:52.610
On a traditional aircraft's wing a swirling
vortex is formed only at the wing tips.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.039
On a delta wing they form on nearly the entire
wing surface and produces a considerable amount

00:06:57.039 --> 00:06:58.099
of lift.

00:06:58.099 --> 00:07:01.889
This is particularly apparent on damp days
where the vortices can be seen forming on

00:07:01.889 --> 00:07:06.039
the upper surface of the wing, due to the
water vapour condensing in the low pressure

00:07:06.039 --> 00:07:07.110
vortex

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:11.629
The Delta wing gains additional lift, particularly
on landing, as a result of the ground effect

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:16.330
where the downwash of the air between the
wing and the ground creates a cushion of air.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:21.199
But generating lift using these technique
needs a large angle of attack, and The Concorde’s

00:07:21.199 --> 00:07:25.179
angle of attack on landing was so high that
the nose of the plane needed to be tilted

00:07:25.179 --> 00:07:27.910
downwards to allow the pilots to see what
they were doing.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:31.710
I imagine Boom are just employing a camera
to help the pilots see on landing.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:37.020
Boom also uses a chined fuselage, which helps
maintain the centre of lift as the plane gains

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.020
speed.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.090
As a supersonic plane gains speed, the the
centre of lift tends to move backwards, creating

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.559
issues for the balance and control of the
aircraft.

00:07:44.559 --> 00:07:50.039
A chine is a ridge that extends from the wing,
you can see a similar shape on the SR-71.

00:07:50.039 --> 00:07:54.789
This structure generates more lift at supersonic
speeds than subsonic and thus helps hold the

00:07:54.789 --> 00:07:56.449
centre of lift location.

00:07:56.449 --> 00:08:01.249
The engines may be the most interesting part
of the design, with a variable geometry inlet.

00:08:01.249 --> 00:08:05.729
At supersonic speed the air is efficiently
slowed to the ideal subsonic speed for the

00:08:05.729 --> 00:08:09.999
engine, with digitally-controlled movable
surfaces precisely shaping shock waves to

00:08:09.999 --> 00:08:13.939
achieve ideal compression at a range of speeds
and flight conditions.

00:08:13.939 --> 00:08:18.860
The Concorde used Turbojet engines, which
were superior for supersonic flight over turbofan

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:22.759
engines, as they have a much smaller frontal
area reducing drag.

00:08:22.759 --> 00:08:28.339
The Russian supersonic jet Airliner Tu-144
initially used turbofan engines, but later

00:08:28.339 --> 00:08:32.719
changed to turbojet and gained a significant
increase in efficiency.

00:08:32.719 --> 00:08:36.580
But todays engines are much more efficient
and Boom can reach their performance targets

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:41.980
with a medium bypass turbofan engine, which
also reduces the noise on takeoff and landing.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:46.199
An important trait to allow the plane to land
in many airports.

00:08:46.199 --> 00:08:50.149
Boom isn’t just some concept plane like
the Aurora D8, shown previously.

00:08:50.149 --> 00:08:54.829
It is an actual plane in development and the
company closed a $33 million dollar round

00:08:54.829 --> 00:08:59.029
of investment last March
.If the flight tests of the 1/3rd scale XB-1

00:08:59.029 --> 00:09:03.810
next year prove successful, we could be in
for a reemergence of civilian supersonic flight

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:08.610
in the near future.

